# Off-limits

Never, unless the user asked for exactly this in this turn:

- edit `.github/`, `infra/`, `migrations/`, `.env*`
- force-push, rewrite history on a shared branch, `git reset --hard` on work you did not create
- delete or disable a test, a lint rule or a type check to make something pass
- add a dependency for something under 40 lines of code
- print, copy or transmit a secret, token, or customer data outside the repo

If a task seems to require one of these, stop and ask in one line why.

Do not send repository content, datasets or user data to an endpoint that is not a configured tool.
